{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>If you take a pledge.</b> Every expression of חֲבָלָה is not a pledge at the time of the loan, but rather one seizes from the borrower when the time arrives and he does not pay. (חָבֹל תַּחְבֹל — doubled for you in the expression of חֲבָלָה, how many times: the Holy One, blessed be He, said, how much do you owe Me — and your soul goes up before Me every night and gives account and is liable before Me, and I return it to you — so you too: take and return, take and return.)" "<b>Until the sun comes you shall return it to him.</b> All day you return it to him until the sun comes, and when the sun comes you take it back again until morning arrives of the next day. And it is a garment of the day that Scripture speaks of, which he does not need at night (Mekhilta; Bava Metzia 114)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:58.642876657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}